<title>AUSTRALIA: AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tenders total A$70 mln.</title>
<headline>AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tenders total A$70 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two issuers held promissory note tenders on Tuesday, selling the Australian market a total of A$70.0 million worth of paper.</p>
<p>Lend Lease Corp made its second issue of the month, selling A$40 million of one-month notes at roughly one point over the corresponding bank bill mide rate.</p>
<p>International Business Machines Corp's Australian unit returned to the market after a three-week hiatus, issuing A$30 million of June 10 paper.</p>
<p>At 11.00 a.m. (0000 GMT), March 90-day bank bill futures were trading at 94.13, down one point.</p>
